{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2658 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "6a56dc9b25849159e8a6b26a83236397015e168b9956efceea947cec9ced9a00" :edb/db-before-t 2657 :edb/db-after-t 2658 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535970 50 #inst "2026-10-09T11:54:06.110Z" 13194139535970 true] [17592186124402 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377326 13194139535970 true] [17592186124402 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377340 13194139535970 true] [17592186124510 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377347 13194139535970 true] [17592186124510 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377354 13194139535970 true] [17592186124549 1020 #edb/ref 17592186377333 13194139535970 true] [17592186377326 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377327 13194139535970 true] [17592186377326 1089 "q-106688" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377326 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535970 true] [17592186377326 1100 "Let $S$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant $1.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\n- The identity matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $S.$\n- For any $A\\in S,$ we can find the corresponding negative matrix $-A\\in S$ such that $A+(-A)=O.$\n- There are matrices $A,B,C\\in S,$ such that $(A+B)+C\\ne A+(B+C).$" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377326 1113 #uuid "4ae15ced-8119-5af5-8ffc-48ebd6ecda50" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377326 1145 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1.$ Hence, $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\in S.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any matrix $A\\in S,$ there is a corresponding negative $2\\times 2$ matrix $-A$ such that\n\n$$\nA+(-A)=A-A=O.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n|-A|=|-1\\cdot A|=(-1)^{2}\\cdot |A|=1\\cdot 1=1,\n$$\n\nhence $-A\\in S.$\n\n- Statement III is false. For any matrices $A,B,C\\in S,$ we have\n\n$$\n(A+B)+C=A+(B+C).\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377327 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377328 13194139535970 true] [17592186377327 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377329 13194139535970 true] [17592186377327 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377330 13194139535970 true] [17592186377327 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377331 13194139535970 true] [17592186377327 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377332 13194139535970 true] [17592186377327 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535970 true] [17592186377327 1041 "selection" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377327 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377331 13194139535970 true] [17592186377327 1110 #uuid "5ca9b6a6-d9cf-5797-968a-b4a9d7b52612" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377328 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377328 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377328 1111 #uuid "84ff2e01-5e8f-539f-a8de-2c9d6e6e074e" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377329 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377329 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377329 1111 #uuid "902ac293-50fe-5dd3-a103-1eb64f244826" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377330 1034 "III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377330 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377330 1111 #uuid "36aad3d0-8ae8-5edd-ae55-22e11ce5fe77" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377331 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377331 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377331 1111 #uuid "e2a5a874-ca88-5ffe-9815-2312da44d691" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377332 1034 "II only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377332 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377332 1111 #uuid "b6450ae3-3fe9-5e6e-87f9-8a22693482e5" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377333 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377334 13194139535970 true] [17592186377333 1089 "q-160872" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377333 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535970 true] [17592186377333 1100 "Let $R$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & a\\end{aligned}],$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\n- ${I}_{2}\\in R$\n- For every $A,B\\in R,$ we have $A+B\\in R.$\n- The set is closed under addition." 13194139535970 true] [17592186377333 1113 #uuid "67eda8f4-5821-5ad3-b3e1-71a69e863a64" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377333 1145 "Let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. The identity matrix ${I}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\in R$ since \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & a\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwith $a=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. There are matrices in $R$ whose sum is *not* in $R.$ For example, let $A=B={I}_{2}.$ Then $A,B\\in R,$  however,\n\n$$\nA+B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\notin R,\n$$\n\nsince the $11$-entry of this resulting matrix is equal to  $2\\ne 1.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is *not* closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377335 13194139535970 true] [17592186377334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377336 13194139535970 true] [17592186377334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377337 13194139535970 true] [17592186377334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377338 13194139535970 true] [17592186377334 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377339 13194139535970 true] [17592186377334 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535970 true] [17592186377334 1041 "selection" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377334 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377336 13194139535970 true] [17592186377334 1110 #uuid "21cd40c9-fae9-5931-9217-5182e2e86430" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377335 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377335 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377335 1111 #uuid "0b35daaf-0f69-52e9-8146-f6a383e476d2" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377336 1034 "I only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377336 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377336 1111 #uuid "f180e510-f31a-5561-8ae7-0a751217583a" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377337 1034 "III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377337 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377337 1111 #uuid "90fbd3d5-1aa8-5d30-98ff-9810f386db3f" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377338 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377338 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377338 1111 #uuid "0922c201-093d-5024-a28a-ad5651311d22" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377339 1034 "II only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377339 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377339 1111 #uuid "bef8ca25-d662-53b6-9abf-203d4c689c84" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377340 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377341 13194139535970 true] [17592186377340 1089 "q-162391" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377340 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535970 true] [17592186377340 1100 "Let $S$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant different from $0.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\n- The  matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $S.$\n- For any $A\\in S,$ we can find the corresponding negative matrix $-A\\in S$ such that $A+(-A)=O.$\n- For any $A,B,C\\in S,$ we have $A+(B-C)=(A+B)-C.$" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377340 1113 #uuid "0744b736-352a-540e-bb81-bc37a57fffc0" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377340 1145 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with real entries,   there is a corresponding negative matrix $-A$ such that\n\n$$\nA+(-A)=A-A=O.\n$$\n\nNotice if $A\\in S$ then \n\n$$\n|-A|=|-1\\cdot A|=(-1)^{2}\\cdot |A|=1\\cdot |A|=|A|\\ne 0,\n$$\n\nhence $-A\\in S.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any matrices $A,B\\in S,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\nA+(B-C)=A+(B+(-C))=(A+B)+(-C)=(A+B)-C\n$$\n\nsince matrix addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377342 13194139535970 true] [17592186377341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377343 13194139535970 true] [17592186377341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377344 13194139535970 true] [17592186377341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377345 13194139535970 true] [17592186377341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377346 13194139535970 true] [17592186377341 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535970 true] [17592186377341 1041 "selection" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377341 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377342 13194139535970 true] [17592186377341 1110 #uuid "c1ff75d3-a8e5-54e0-98cc-9134944a954e" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377342 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377342 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377342 1111 #uuid "aa0e5350-2123-5661-83b4-144547d868fd" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377343 1034 "I only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377343 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377343 1111 #uuid "59ec396a-877f-5c2e-a9fe-50df6343929c" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377344 1034 "III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377344 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377344 1111 #uuid "71b86d0d-9538-5759-83ba-e0871735cc0b" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377345 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377345 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377345 1111 #uuid "2ce6051c-1a12-5842-aa60-a56eb030ad64" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377346 1034 "II only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377346 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377346 1111 #uuid "0707807a-07fe-52d5-a740-f533f71f24d9" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377347 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377348 13194139535970 true] [17592186377347 1089 "q-94700" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377347 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535970 true] [17592186377347 1100 "Let $R$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\n- For any $A\\in R,$ we have $1\\cdot A=A.$\n- For any $A\\in R,$ we have $-1(-1\\cdot A)=-A.$\n- For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377347 1113 #uuid "0fa43ff8-a4bd-5dc5-820b-bc6dfbc6db69" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377347 1145 "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in R$ with real entries, we have\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {a}_{ij}={a}_{ij}\n$$\n\nand, hence,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot A=A.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ from $R.$  Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1(-1\\cdot A) & =-1(-1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =-1([\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot 1 & (-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 0 & (-1)\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =-1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-1) & (-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 0 & (-1)\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A\\ne -A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements III is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in R,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta ){a}_{ij}=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+\\beta {a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377348 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377349 13194139535970 true] [17592186377348 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377350 13194139535970 true] [17592186377348 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377351 13194139535970 true] [17592186377348 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377352 13194139535970 true] [17592186377348 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377353 13194139535970 true] [17592186377348 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535970 true] [17592186377348 1041 "selection" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377348 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377350 13194139535970 true] [17592186377348 1110 #uuid "d5a86d18-b59d-59f1-8413-fa691575a06e" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377349 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377349 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377349 1111 #uuid "37bc121e-b726-5883-a5b2-33a0cc135e30" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377350 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377350 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377350 1111 #uuid "40e2648d-3e02-59f0-be5e-1f8130ebec7d" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377351 1034 "I only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377351 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377351 1111 #uuid "c9e5fa3f-4bcb-5d20-aecb-cb89813c1179" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377352 1034 "III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377352 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377352 1111 #uuid "912c1922-c3a3-5a71-9fa9-f47272841e3c" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377353 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377353 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377353 1111 #uuid "68ecac35-4358-5bd6-a170-ce6879f8fc6a" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377354 1017 #edb/ref 17592186377355 13194139535970 true] [17592186377354 1089 "q-94723" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377354 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535970 true] [17592186377354 1100 "Let $T$ be the set of polynomials of the form $ax+2,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $2x\\in T.$\n- The scalar multiplication of polynomials in $T$ is associative.\n- For any $p(x)\\in T$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).$" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377354 1113 #uuid "fe7eb437-c49e-5d72-9bf5-386650b87dda" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377354 1145 "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $T$ contains only polynomials of the form $ax+2,$ where $a$ is a real coefficient. However, $2x$ is not a polynomial of this form. So, $2x\\notin T.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in T$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta p(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )p(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in T$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )p(x)=\\alpha p(x)+\\beta p(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377356 13194139535970 true] [17592186377355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377357 13194139535970 true] [17592186377355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377358 13194139535970 true] [17592186377355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377359 13194139535970 true] [17592186377355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377360 13194139535970 true] [17592186377355 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535970 true] [17592186377355 1041 "selection" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377355 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377356 13194139535970 true] [17592186377355 1110 #uuid "fdc5419d-eb1f-54ff-adcc-5bc70388ef65" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377356 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377356 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377356 1111 #uuid "20e9adc8-3918-5315-a6ff-e82c12a245a9" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377357 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377357 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 true] [17592186377357 1111 #uuid "401b334b-5597-5b5f-82a4-25df094c9535" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377358 1034 "III only" 13194139535970 true] [17592186377358 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535970 tr